#### Controls for QGP Effects in Heavy-Ion Measurements

Measurements of jets, heavy flavor, and flow open avenues to study the QGP. However, additional controls are also needed. Once a jet or heavy flavor observable has been measured, it is important to be able to compare it to some benchmark to be able to disentangle what parts of the signal, if any, are from a QGP. Observe, for example, the cartoon of processes in Figure 1.7.22 Many effects can result from both the pre-equilibrium state and in the hadron gas phase which are shared in both versions of collision evolution - with or without a QGP - whose signals are not trivial to separate from QGP signals.

